window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["06"]={"https://theconversation.com/sentinels-is-an-urgent-call-to-action-on-bird-flu-and-capitalism-gone-wild-its-also-a-joy-to-read-293348":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"27a8192075e6e7ac403d5246eb0d0250fdcdfeabfd9a79e33eec8109f68c8d88","read":"https://theconversation.com/sentinels-is-an-urgent-call-to-action-on-bird-flu-and-capitalism-gone-wild-its-also-a-joy-to-read-293348","bytes":189535,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Sentinels is an urgent call to action on bird flu, and capitalism gone wild. It’s also a joy to read","by":[{"n":"Euan Ritchie","r":"Professor in Wildlife Ecology and Conservation, School of Life & Environmental Sciences, Deakin University"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T18:24:34Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Highly pathogenic avian influenza (H5N1 bird flu) is the defining disease of our times, suggests Australian writer and journalist ",["Michael Dulaney","https://michael-dulaney.com/"]," in his timely book ",["Sentinels","https://scribepublications.com.au/books/sentinels"],", on what happens when diseases spread between animals and humans."]},{"k":"p","s":["Now ",["impacting mainland Australian wildlife","https://theconversation.com/bird-flu-has-spread-to-two-australian-states-heres-how-it-could-accelerate-our-extinction-crisis-285807"],", the disease, which reached us in June, epitomises our callous neglect of nature, despite us being embedded in and reliant on it."]},{"k":"p","s":["“Of all the pathogens I’ve learned about, this is the big one,” Dulaney writes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Review: Sentinels by Michael Dulaney (Scribe Publications)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Over ",["700 bird flu events","https://www.agriculture.gov.au/campaigns/birdflu/latest-data#introduction_data"]," – which cover individual or multiple deaths of animals – have occurred in Australia so far. Greater crested terns, little penguins, common bottlenose dolphin, long-nosed fur seals, Australian sea lions, and many other bird and mammal species have all succumbed. It’s a sobering result ",["of our missed chances","https://theconversation.com/australias-bird-flu-response-too-little-but-its-not-too-late-290045"]," to protect nature and prevent pathogens from jumping between non-human animals and people."]},{"k":"p","s":["In his book, which was longlisted for this year’s ",["Walkley Book Award","https://www.walkleys.com/awards/walkleys/walkley-book-award/"]," and published just a few months after bird flu reached Australia, Dulaney thoughtfully discusses our impacts on and connections with non-human life. We continue to exploit species and plunder nature at an alarming scale and rate. It’s estimated humans exploit as much as ",["300 times more species","https://www.nature.com/articles/s42003-023-04940-w"]," than non-human predators."]},{"k":"p","s":["The concept of a sentinel — the canary in the coal mine — draws from epidemiology, the study of disease. Dulaney’s thesis is that these sentinels are increasingly sickly, often dropping dead at disturbingly regular rates and in extraordinary numbers. It’s hard to dispute this."]},{"k":"p","s":["A recent grisly example is the estimated death of more than 13,000 elephant seal pups, ",["more than 75% of all pups born","https://www.antarctica.gov.au/news/2026/scientists-determine-extent-of-h5-avian-influenza-bird-flu-outbreak-at-heard-island-and-mcdonald-islands/"],", on the sub-Antarctic ",["Heard Island","https://www.antarctica.gov.au/antarctic-operations/stations-and-field-locations/heard-island/"]," last summer, as their remote, isolated location and shielding from H5N1 bird flu were inevitably breached. Humans are destroying nature and the spillover of diseases that jump between species – including to and from humans – is increasing. Dulaney writes:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Researchers have counted around 200 new infectious diseases that have broken out more than 12,000 times over the past three decades On average, one new infectious disease jumps to humans every eight months."]},{"k":"p","s":["He suggests this threat should be considered in the same way as other globally significant and existential threats, including climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a wildlife ecologist and conservation scientist, I echo his call to action."]},{"k":"h","s":["A joy to read"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sentinels is composed of three parts and eight chapters. The first part is focused on wildlife, the second on agriculture and the third looks at the impacts of commerce, the wildlife trade and our treatment of fellow human beings."]},{"k":"p","s":["One chilling passage describes how in California’s bulging prison population, one of five of the state’s cases of ",["Valley fever","https://theconversation.com/fungal-infections-known-as-valley-fever-could-spike-this-fall-3-epidemiologists-explain-how-to-protect-yourself-238972"]," (a disease caused by pathogenic fungi) was found among its prisoners between 2007 and 2011."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dulaney’s writing is a joy. Easily consumed, complex ideas and information are made accessible to the reader. Sentinels is very well referenced too, including extensive peer-reviewed research. Case studies span China, the Andes, the Arctic, Indonesia, Australia and elsewhere. As a result, this book is undoubtedly globally relevant."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dulaney also takes his readers to the front lines. There are stories of ecologists studying flying foxes in forests, and about the relevance of ",["Hendra virus","https://www.who.int/health-topics/hendra-virus-infection#tab=tab_1"],", which causes severe, often fatal disease in both infected horses and humans. It can pass from bats to horses, and has killed people working with horses."]},{"k":"p","s":["Elsewhere, the book details people trying to protect endangered amphibians on Indonesian mountains, as Dulaney spends four days with Angga, a gifted wildlife tracker. “Sometimes, when Angga uncovers an exceptionally rare frog or snake species, his clients break down crying over finding something they have searched for their whole lives,” he writes."]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s even discussion of the potential links between pigs, East Germany and the fall of communism."]},{"k":"p","s":["The epilogue is perhaps the most powerful and vital section of the book. It brings together how what’s happening is not a case of misfortune, but a predictable, likely outcome of what we’re doing: the habitats we destroy, and the crowding of people and animals."]},{"k":"p","s":["The science is clear. Our actions are stressing wildlife populations and in some cases, they bring wildlife and their diseases closer to us and the animals we farm and eat. It’s a recipe for disaster. The increasing reliance of flying foxes on urban environments to find food – and the Hendra virus risk this poses – is because we’ve destroyed large areas of forests and woodlands these animals relied upon."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dulaney comes hard at capitalism, too, pointing to its commodification of nature. This will likely rankle some – but again, it’s hard to argue against. Even within the conservation community I’m part of, the value of species and ecosystems are often framed and described through the services they provide us, rather than their intrinsic value. The Australian government now has a ",["Nature repair market","https://theconversation.com/the-government-hopes-private-investors-will-help-save-nature-heres-how-its-scheme-could-fail-193010"],", which includes the use of ",["controversial offsets","https://www.youngausint.org.au/post/australia-s-nature-repair-market-was-never-meant-to-be-an-offsets-scheme"]," that allow for further environmental destruction."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dulaney is clear about his ecological grief. “In the days prior to handling ducks, I’d watched distressing video compilations filmed by carers around the world who could do nothing but witness these slow deaths,” he writes about bird flu. In the chapter devoted to it, he writes:"]},{"k":"p","s":["I have come to believe that bird flu is the archetypal disease of this new age, the one that represents all of our failed efforts to address the growing threat of spillover – a disease that links farming, unrestrained industry, political intransigience, and environmental exploitation in a way that threatens hundreds of species, including our own. It scares me more than anything else."]},{"k":"p","s":["His honesty and authenticity mean Sentinels rises above many science-based books I’ve read, which clumsily attempt to hide the authors’ personal views and values. We are not impartial automatons: we all have skin in this game, which concerns our only home. Dulaney makes the case for urgent and substantial change."]},{"k":"h","s":["Hope, but no sugarcoating"]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of the book is confronting; Dulaney does not sugarcoat our predicament. But he offers hope – and makes the important point that tackling disease will also help address other crises, such as climate change, which are inextricably linked."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sentinels covers a lot of ground. Given the complexities of disease ecology and the wicked problem of managing wildlife and societies to reduce our exposure to pandemics and better protect biodiversity, it’s unsurprising some issues aren’t covered in the depth I might desire. But in my view, this is more than compensated for by the broad knowledge and understanding readers will get from Dulaney’s book."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sentinels is a vital read. I hope it reaches a diverse audience, including our political leaders, who need to confront the challenges it so thoughtfully describes. To protect ourselves, we must protect our ecosystems and the species that sustain them."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ongoing demise of wildlife and the global rise of diseases and pandemics sound clarion calls we must urgently act upon. We must improve our relationship with nature."]}],"chars":7260},"https://theconversation.com/cabo-verdes-presidential-election-the-stakes-in-one-of-africas-most-stable-democracies-295763":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"da87c4ab39224dc02448f9abc79d6b694a4b1396b165fae2bbec6a867ee3eee4","read":"https://theconversation.com/cabo-verdes-presidential-election-the-stakes-in-one-of-africas-most-stable-democracies-295763","bytes":179680,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Cabo Verde’s presidential election: the stakes in one of Africa’s most stable democracies","by":[{"n":"José Santana Pereira","r":"associate professor, researcher, Universidade de Lisboa"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T13:19:33Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Cabo Verde’s ",["presidential election","https://www.ecowas.int/ecowas-deploys-a-long-term-election-observation-mission-in-the-republic-of-cabo-verde-2/"]," takes place against the backdrop of a ",["democratic record","https://freedomhouse.org/country/cabo-verde/freedom-world/2026"]," that remains unusual in its regional context. The country, made up of an archipelago of islands off the coast of west Africa, has sustained multiparty competition for more than three decades. It has had peaceful transfers of power and no coups or military takeovers since independence from ",["Portugal in 1975","https://www.britannica.com/place/Cabo-Verde/Struggle-for-independence"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cabo Verde (population ",["530,000","https://ourworldindata.org/profile/population-demography/cape-verde"],") is a semi-presidential republic in which the president is directly elected. The prime minister is appointed by the president in light of parliamentary election results, and heads a government that is politically accountable to the national assembly."]},{"k":"p","s":["The president represents the state and safeguards the constitution, while the prime minister and the government conduct public policy."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["presidency","https://www.parlamento.cv/Constituicao/"]," nevertheless carries substantial political weight. The president can veto legislation, request constitutional review and, under ",["certain conditions","https://www.parlamento.cv/Constituicao/"],", dissolve parliament. The office also entails responsibilities in foreign affairs and national defence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The president is, therefore, not the principal policymaker. However, the way in which these powers are exercised can become particularly consequential when the president and prime minister belong to opposing political camps. This might indeed be the outcome of the 15 November 2026 election."]},{"k":"p","s":["I am a political communication specialist who has researched ",["the dynamics of Cabo Verde’s presidential elections","https://journals.openedition.org/cea/4331?lang=en"],". In my view the central test for the upcoming poll will be whether the country’s institutions can continue to function effectively while preserving the important distinction between the presidency and the government."]},{"k":"h","s":["The background"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cabo Verde’s political climate is shaped by a ",["recent change of government","https://www.idea.int/democracytracker/report/cabo-verde/may-2026"],". The African Party for the Independence of Cabo Verde returned to office after winning the May 2026 parliamentary election. This ",["ended 10 years of government","https://www.internazionale.it/ultime-notizie-reuters/2026/05/18/cape-verde-ruling-party-unseated-in-election-partial-results-show"]," by the Movement for Democracy, which now forms the opposition."]},{"k":"p","s":["The African Party for the Independence of Cabo Verde’s victory reflected growing ",["voter dissatisfaction","https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/cape-verde-ruling-party-unseated-election-partial-results-show-2026-05-18/"]," with a decade of rule by the Movement for Democracy. This is particularly over poor inter-island transport, economic difficulties, living conditions and public security."]},{"k":"p","s":["The change of government renewed questions about ",["the balance of power","https://africacenter.org/spotlight/en-elections-2026/caboverde/"]," between the president, the new government and parliament, as well as the opposition’s ability to hold the ruling party accountable."]},{"k":"p","s":["The forthcoming presidential election will, therefore, test not only party loyalties but also voters’ expectations of the presidency and its role in the political system."]},{"k":"p","s":["The two main contenders are ",["José Maria Neves","https://www.britannica.com/place/Cabo-Verde/Struggle-for-independence#ref1298722"],", backed by the African Party for the Independence of Cabo Verde, and ",["Joana Rosa","https://cabo-verde.cv/joana-rosa-first-female-presidential-candidate-in-cape-verde/"],", supported by the Movement for Democracy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Neves previously served as prime minister between 2001 and 2016. Rosa, a former minister of justice, is the first woman to run for president in Cabo Verde."]},{"k":"p","s":["They face ",["Antero Tavares","https://www.wathi.org/candidat-election-cap-vert-2026/antero-lucio-lopes-frances-tavares-candidat-independant/"],", ",["Casimiro de Pina","https://www.brava.news/en/casimiro-de-pina-announces-candidacy-for-presidency-of-the-republic-in-the-2026-elections"],", ",["Gilson Alves","https://cabo-verde.cv/cape-verde-candidate-investigated-for-inciting-crime/"]," and ",["Loisito Sousa","https://www.wathi.org/candidat-election-cap-vert-2026/loisito-tavares-de-sousa-candidat-independant/"],". These four offer alternatives to the two parties that have dominated national politics since the introduction of multipartyism in 1991."]},{"k":"p","s":["These candidates are unlikely, however, to attract support on a scale that would challenge the two main contenders."]},{"k":"h","s":["The voters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Together with political science researchers Danielton Delgado and Susana Rogeiro Nina, I published a paper that offers insight into the dynamics of presidential elections in Cabo Verde. ",["Our 2019 study","https://journals.openedition.org/cea/4331?lang=en"]," found that voters didn’t consistently use presidential contests to punish the governing party. Indeed, except in 2011 and 2021, every presidential election in the country was won by the candidate backed by the party that controlled parliament and the executive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Also, there was not a systematic advantage for independent candidates or candidates backed by smaller parties. The short interval – ",["one to six months","https://africacenter.org/spotlight/2021-elections/"]," – between legislative and presidential elections may help explain this phenomenon, as presidential contests often take place during the governing party’s post-election “honeymoon period”."]},{"k":"h","s":["What’s different in the upcoming election?"]},{"k":"p","s":["If Neves secures re-election, the presidency and government will be held by figures associated with the same party. This possibility is not unlikely. Since the introduction of multiparty democracy in 1991, every incumbent president who has sought a second term has been re-elected: ",["António Mascarenhas Monteiro","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Antonio-Mascarenhas-Monteiro"]," in 1996, ",["Pedro Pires","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Pedro-Pires"]," in 2006 and ",["Jorge Carlos Fonseca","https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/jorge-carlos-fonseca-president-of-cape-verde-world-leaders-in-history.html"]," in 2016."]},{"k":"p","s":["A victory for Neves could play out in one of two ways. It could facilitate cooperation, but it could also raise questions about the president’s independence from the government."]},{"k":"p","s":["In turn, a victory for Rosa, mirroring the patterns that emerged in 2011 and 2021, would create a situation of divided leadership, with a Movement for Democracy-backed president working alongside an African Party for the Independence of Cabo Verde government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such an arrangement is not inherently problematic. Nevertheless, it can require negotiation when constitutional responsibilities and political interests diverge."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cabo Verde has recent experience of this situation: between November 2021 and the formation of the new government in June 2026, Neves dealt with a Movement for Democracy government. This was led by ",["Ulisses Correia e Silva","https://concordia.net/community/his-excellency-jose-ulisses-correia-e-silva/"],". Despite their partisan differences, relations were generally characterised by institutional cooperation rather than open confrontation."]},{"k":"p","s":["In short, whoever wins will face a distinct institutional challenge. Neves will have to balance his party affiliation with the constitutional responsibility to act as head of state. Rosa will need to establish a working relationship with a government led by her political opponents."]}],"chars":5757},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cuba":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"a47d60bf5e7ed970441460aba14f7e9e4f3eb3251a8c617af187d634a3b60e6b","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/cuba","bytes":73629,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Cuba travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-19T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-09-25T12:36:31+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Cuba"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests in Cuba"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cuba is experiencing a worsening economic situation with shortages of fuel, electricity, water and basic necessities. This is affecting tourism services and disrupting travel within the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation has led to frequent protests. To date most of these have remained peaceful but be aware that protests can escalate. You should stay away from large gatherings, monitor the media for updates and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation is also leading to an increase in opportunistic crime, but levels remain lower than in the UK. See ‘Crime’ on the ",["Safety and security page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cuba/safety-and-security#crime"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Power outages and fuel and water shortages"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Cuban National Electric grid has collapsed a number of times over the last few months. Given current circumstances, further grid collapses are likely. Low fuel reserves are leading to severe and sustained disruption to essential infrastructure and basic services, including transport, medical care, communications, water supply and street lighting. Authorities have introduced fuel rationing, scaled back public services, and made changes to healthcare, education, transport and tourism operations to conserve severely limited energy supplies. Access to safe drinking water and wastewater management can be problematic."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take precautions by conserving fuel, water, food and mobile phone charge, and be prepared for significant disruption."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel disruption"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cuban authorities have announced that all of its international airports are without aviation fuel. Only Terminal 3 at José Martí International Airport is currently in operation. Some airlines, including all Canadian airlines, Air France, Iberia, World2Fly and LATAM, have suspended flights to and from Cuba. Other airlines are keeping their routes under review. Options for leaving the country could reduce further if the situation worsens."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are currently in Cuba, carefully consider if your presence is essential. The situation has the potential to deteriorate quickly and without warning. Make sure you are ready to change your plans quickly if needed. If you are considering leaving Cuba, check for messaging from your airline or tour operator for up-to-date information. Ensure your travel documents remain valid and confirm you have any required visas for onward travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Continue to monitor local media and follow the instructions of local authorities. Subscribe to ",["FCDO email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cuba/email-signup"]," and read our ",["guidance on how to deal with a crisis overseas","https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/support-for-british-nationals-abroad#help-in-a-crisis"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["International card transactions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Cuban Central Bank has announced that international cards such as Visa and Mastercard are no longer accepted in Cuba. Available payment methods include cash and Cuban prepaid cards. You will not be able to withdraw cash through ATMs with an international card."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to visit Cuba, you should bring enough cash to cover your expenses for the entire length of your stay and in case of an emergency (such as medical treatment or delayed departure). US dollars and euros are widely accepted and can be exchanged in Cuba. See ‘Money’ on the ",["Safety and security page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cuba/safety-and-security#money"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency. Make sure your travel insurance covers Cuba."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cuba/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Cuba’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Cuba set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Cuban Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Cuba, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and 3 months after your planned departure date."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting Cuba as a tourist, you need to get a tourist visa, also known as a tourist card, before you travel. Apply through the ",["Cuban Embassy in the UK","https://misiones.cubaminrex.cu/en/united-kingdom/embassy-cuba-united-kingdom-great-britain-and-northern-ireland"]," or check with your travel agent or tour operator. You can also apply for an electronic visa through the ",["eVisa-Cuba","https://evisacuba.cu/en/inicio"]," site. When your application is approved, you will receive a ten-character code which should be entered as you fill in your advance passenger information on the ",["DViajeros","https://www.dviajeros.mitrans.gob.cu/inicio"]," platform (see below). This will generate a QR code to be presented to the immigration authorities at the border. The electronic visa will be linked to the applicant’s passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must also show proof of onward or return travel. See ",["Cuba’s consular services information","https://misiones.cubaminrex.cu/en/united-kingdom/consular-services"]," for details."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information and advice about other types of visas, contact the ",["Cuban Embassy in the UK","https://misiones.cubaminrex.cu/en/united-kingdom/embassy-cuba-united-kingdom-great-britain-and-northern-ireland"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Overstaying your visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities take any breach of immigration rules seriously. You could be detained if you overstay your visa."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must complete an online arrival form on the ",["D’Viajeros traveller information portal","https://dviajeros.mitrans.gob.cu/inicio"]," within 72 hours before entering the country. You’ll get a QR code by email. This must be shown to the authorities on arrival as an electronic or printed version. Airlines will check completion of the form at check-in."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should download or print your completed ",["DViajeros","https://www.dviajeros.mitrans.gob.cu/inicio"]," form as a PDF, as wifi may not be accessible to do so on arrival in Cuba."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling from the USA to Cuba"]},{"k":"p","s":["US regulations do not authorise tourist travel to Cuba from the US. Travellers departing the US for Cuba are generally required to certify that their travel falls within one of the 12 categories for which the US authorities approve direct travel to Cuba."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information see the ",["US State Department’s travel advice for Cuba","https://travel.state.gov/content/passports/en/country/cuba.html"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling from Cuba to the USA"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot travel from Cuba to the USA without a US visa."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Cuba guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/60/cuba#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are rules about the types of ",["goods you can take into and out of Cuba","https://www.cubatravel.cu/en/useful-information/regulations-and-formalities"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Art and antiques"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some art and antiques require an export permit from the Country Heritage Office (‘Bienes Culturales’). Ask the vendor if they have the required permit for the item you are buying. At the airport, you may need to show the receipt."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Photography equipment"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need an import licence for photography equipment, as well as the appropriate journalism visa."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["You are not allowed to bring drones into Cuba. They will be confiscated on arrival and not returned until your departure. The process for getting your drone back could be lengthy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Food items"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take meat products, milk, fresh fruit, vegetables, seeds or organic matter into Cuba, with ",["some exceptions","https://www.aduana.gob.cu/en/basic-page/phytosanitary-and-veterinary-provisions"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Electrical items and GPS on mobiles"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some electrical items with heavy power consumption may be confiscated on entry to Cuba."]},{"k":"p","s":["Global Positioning Systems (GPS) are subject to import requirements. Mobile phones, tablets and laptops can be taken to Cuba, but you must turn off any inbuilt GPS."]},{"k":"p","s":["Complete a customs form if items are confiscated on your arrival so you can collect them on your departure date."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Cuba"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Cuban national peso (CUP ‘moneda nacional’) is the official currency and cannot be exchanged outside of Cuba. Declare foreign currency you’re taking into Cuba if the value is more than 5,000 US dollars."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to exchange money anywhere other than Cadeca exchange houses. See ‘Money’ on the ",["Safety and security page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cuba/safety-and-security#money"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Cuba"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Cuba, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cuba is ruled by a single party, with a high level of social control. Opposition parties are not allowed. There are restrictions on freedom of speech, association and assembly for Cuban nationals. Any political demonstrations not approved by the government may be broken up by the authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid any demonstrations or large gatherings and follow the advice of the local authorities. Internet access can sometime be blocked during times of political tension."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["While crime has reportedly increased in recently months, data suggests that levels of crime are generally lower than in the UK or regional averages, but the difficult economic situation is leading to an increase in opportunistic crime. There have been reports of muggings in Havana and of burglaries at properties, with instances of violent crime. Siphoning of fuel from parked vehicles is a regular occurrence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Exercise caution, particularly at night. Keep your personal belongings, including your passport, in a secure place, avoid carrying large amounts of cash or showing signs of affluence. Always carry a photocopy of your passport. Pre-arrange transport and avoid walking at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of theft from luggage when baggage is being handled on arrival or departure at the airport. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not pack valuables in your hold luggage"]},{"k":"li","s":["lock suitcases"]},{"k":"li","s":["shrink-wrap luggage before check-in if possible"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of pickpockets and bag-snatching:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the streets of Old Havana or any crowded areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["on public transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["in nightclubs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not carry large amounts of cash or wear expensive-looking jewellery. Mobiles and laptops are particularly attractive to thieves. Leave valuables in a hotel safe."]},{"k":"p","s":["Beware of theft from your accommodation, particularly from private guest houses (‘casas particulares’)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fake taxi drivers"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are a small number of criminals who pose as tour operators or taxi drivers. These fake drivers operate at the airport and around Old Havana. Only travel with your tour operator. If you need to use a taxi from the airport, make sure it’s a registered yellow taxi."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are sometimes car-related crimes and muggings in Havana, and other tourist areas. Do not hail taxis or accept lifts from anyone you do not know. Take care when driving in central Havana, particularly at night. Keep doors locked and windows closed."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been attacks on foreigners in hire cars after deliberate puncturing of tyres. If you are in a remote area with a punctured tyre drive on to the nearest town before stopping. Do not pick up hitchhikers."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cuba has a zero tolerance policy against the use, possession and trafficking of illegal drugs. Cuban courts can give severe penalties for drug-related offences. Pack all luggage yourself and do not carry items for anyone else."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in restricted areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid all military zones and other restricted areas. Do not take photographs or videos in these areas. Possession of photographs or information relating to military areas or installations can be regarded as espionage and could result in a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Cuba, but gender diversity is not fully accepted by the general population. Same-sex marriages are recognised under Cuban law."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Risk of detention"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you break the law, or are suspected of causing injury to someone, you may be stopped from leaving Cuba during the investigation and trial, and you could be imprisoned. Contact the ",["British Embassy in Havana","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-havana"]," as soon as possible for assistance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Cuban Central Bank has announced that international cards such as Visa and Mastercard are no longer accepted in Cuba. Available payment methods include cash and Cuban prepaid cards (CLASICA card). You will not be able to withdraw cash through ATMs with an international card."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to visit Cuba, you should bring enough cash to cover your expenses for the entire length of your stay and in case of an emergency (including medical costs or if your departure is delayed). US dollars and euros are widely accepted and can be exchanged in Cuba."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to exchange money anywhere other than Cadeca exchange houses, including with any individuals who may offer exchange services. If you’re caught making an unauthorised exchange, you could be fined or get a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your hotel and tour providers on how to make payments ahead of your arrival in Cuba, and whether these can be made in advance via international bank transfer. Take precautions when carrying large amounts of cash."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Cuba with a UK driving licence for up to 6 months. After 6 months, you must pass a driving test and get a Cuban driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can hire a car in Cuba, but fuel shortages can make it difficult to get petrol or diesel, especially for long distances. If you hire a car with a driver, they may know where to source fuel but supply is intermittent."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Motorcycles and scooters"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you hire a moped or motorbike, check the condition of the vehicle carefully. All drivers and passengers must wear a crash helmet."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Three-wheel Coco-taxis may be in an unsafe condition. Tourists have been injured and killed when riding in these vehicles."]},{"k":"p","s":["App-based taxi services are available but Wi-Fi and data signal is limited. Pre-book a return journey if possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Official yellow taxis are generally reliable. Avoid private taxis and old private classic taxi cars as it is unlikely that they will be properly licensed or have modern safety features. It is best to book rides in old classic cars from reputable companies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are variable. Many vehicles, including public transport, are badly maintained. Drivers are prone to stop suddenly and may not signal. There is little if any street lighting at night and roads are badly sign-posted. Avoid driving at night as animals and unlit vehicles are a danger and you may not see hazards such as potholes."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The hurricane season in Cuba is from June to November each year. Heavy rains often cause flash floods and landslides. After a hurricane, power, communications and water supplies can be disrupted. In extreme weather conditions, flights to and from Cuba may be delayed or cancelled. Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a result of Hurricane Melissa in October 2025, infrastructure and services, including access to electricity and water, remain severely impacted in the East of Cuba."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cuba is in an active earthquake zone, but strong earthquakes are not common. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 104 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ambulance service is limited and generally unreliable, particularly in emergencies outside urban areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Cuba","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/60/cuba#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The Cuban government had declared an arbovirus epidemic in 2025 following the significant increase in cases of mosquito-borne diseases in Cuba, including Dengue, Oropouche and Chikungunya. Although the epidemic warning is no longer live, these viruses continue to circulate. The U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) has ",["issued a notice","https://wwwnc.cdc.gov/travel/notices/level2/chikungunya-cuba"]," (“Practice Enhanced Precautions”) in response to a Chikungunya outbreak in Cuba."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Cuba,","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/60/cuba"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["oropouche virus disease"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should take precautions to avoid or prevent mosquito and other insect bites."]},{"k":"p","s":["To control the spread of mosquito-borne diseases, the Cuban authorities may carry out chemical fumigation measures across the island. The chemicals used may cause some discomfort if you come into contact with them."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe shortages of basic medicines, but clinics treating foreigners are more likely to stock basic medical supplies. Many medicines, pharmacy items and sanitary products that are easily accessible in the UK, are not available in Cuba."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a pre-existing medical condition, do not expect to buy medication in Cuba. A letter from your GP stating treatment and dosage may be helpful if you need treatment from a medical practitioner."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries. Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Cuba"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in Havana are better than elsewhere in Cuba. If you need medical treatment, you or your insurance company will need to pay with foreign currency (most likely USD) before any treatment, bearing in mind that Visa/Mastercard payments cannot be made. Make sure you have accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Cuba","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cuba-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Psychiatric care facilities for foreigners are limited and difficult to access."]},{"k":"p","s":[["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Cuba"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 104"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 105"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 106"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Cuba"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Cuba"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Cuba"]," in Cuba"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Cuba","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/when-someone-dies-in-cuba"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Cuba","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cuba-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/cuba/british-embassy-havana"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cuba/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Cuba","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-cuba"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":21134,"change":"This travel advice has been reviewed for accuracy with changes made throughout, including protests in Cuba, power outages and fuel and water shortages, travel disruption, international card transactions, travel insurance, visa requirements, travelling to the USA from Cuba, taking money into Cuba, cr"},"https://theconversation.com/your-first-home-government-loan-scheme-for-first-time-buyers-could-strain-an-already-punishing-property-market-295802":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"4ffdf87496456345c6966db249b1c16c14986971be4a60ba6c7470b7c2ca20c9","read":"https://theconversation.com/your-first-home-government-loan-scheme-for-first-time-buyers-could-strain-an-already-punishing-property-market-295802","bytes":183660,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Your First Home: government loan scheme for first-time buyers could strain an already punishing property market","by":[{"n":"Corinna Elsenbroich","r":"Reader in Computational Modelling, University of Glasgow"},{"n":"Nigel Gilbert","r":"Professor of Sociology, University of Surrey"},{"n":"Yahya Gamal","r":"Research Associate (Urban Intelligence & Analytics), University of Glasgow"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T13:20:02Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Housing in the UK has become markedly less affordable over the last 25 years. Between 2000 and 2025, English house prices rose by about 250% in cash terms (roughly 85% in real terms), while median earnings only doubled in cash terms, and rose by around ",["10% in real terms","https://landregistry.data.gov.uk/app/ukhpi/browse?from=2000-01-01&location=http%3A%2F%2Flandregistry.data.gov.uk%2Fid%2Fregion%2Funited-kingdom&to=2026-01-01&lang=en"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The median English house price is now over seven times median full-time earnings, ",["up from around four in 2000","https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/housing/bulletins/housingaffordabilityinenglandandwales/2025"],". The increasing disconnect between house prices and wage growth is hitting first-time buyers particularly hard."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mortgage deposits present the biggest hurdle to getting on the property ladder. While deposits varied until the 2008 financial crisis, ",["20% deposits have been the norm since 2009","https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/housing/bulletins/mortgagestatisticsuk/2025"]," – now an insurmountable barrier for most first-time buyers."]},{"k":"p","s":["To address this problem, the UK government keeps reaching for the same fix: equity loan schemes for first-time buyers. The first of these was the 2013-2023 Help to Buy scheme in England. The UK government announced its successor, Your First Home, in September 2026. It will be available from February 2027."]},{"k":"p","s":["The goal of these schemes is noble, but supporting market entry in this way could potentially pour fuel onto an already overheating market. This was exactly what happened with Help to Buy, which offered first-time buyers a government loan of up to 20% of a new-build property’s price (40% in London from 2016). Buyers had to provide a 5% deposit."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The government’s evaluation report","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/evaluation-of-the-help-to-buy-scheme/evaluation-of-the-help-to-buy-scheme-evaluation-findings-report"]," showed that the scheme supported over 387,000 purchases. It also stimulated housebuilding – around 15% of all new dwellings built in England from 2013 to 2023 are attributable to the scheme."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the report also finds that it contributed to higher house prices, as it raised the purchasing power of house buyers without substantially increasing the number of homes. Comparing prices in the Wales/England border region, prices were around 2% higher on the English side, where Help to Buy was introduced one year ahead of Wales."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labour’s new Your First Home scheme was announced in September and ratified in the ",["October budget","https://theconversation.com/budget-2026-experts-on-what-john-healeys-breathing-space-plan-means-for-households-295377"],", amid ",["accusations","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cv8e33gdw17no"]," that it will have the same effect. Ministers claim that Your First Home will avoid the pitfalls of its predecessor through income caps, targeting the scheme at those that cannot get some or all of the deposit from their parents (the “bank of mum and dad”)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your First Home gives first-time buyers of new builds a 20% equity loan (40% in London), interest-free for the first five years, with regional price caps. Buyers only need a minimum deposit of 2.5%, cannot provide more than a 15% deposit, and there is a household income cap of £110,000 (or £140,000 in London)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Help to Buy included no income caps, and buyers needed a 5% deposit (with no upper cap). Despite these changes, Your First Home will likely have the same impact."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["The real reason abolishing stamp duty won’t help first-time buyers","https://theconversation.com/the-real-reason-abolishing-stamp-duty-wont-help-first-time-buyers-267584"]]},{"k":"h","s":["No meaningful difference"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Our research","https://doi.org/10.18564/jasss.5518"]," has tested the effect of these changes to equity loans in a computational model of the English housing market. We found that there is no material difference in market effects between the two schemes: both lead to the same kinds of price increases for owner-occupier homes."]},{"k":"p","s":["We tested some hypotheses in model experiments. We looked at whether house price inflation could be curbed through better targeting – either through the lower deposit requirement or different salary caps. We also tested the effects of restricting eligibility to new homes only."]},{"k":"p","s":["We found that reducing the buyer deposit from 5% to 2.5% made no significant difference in house price outcomes: both stimulated the market equally. However, salary caps had the potential to curb house price inflation, but they had to be relatively low."]},{"k":"p","s":["A salary cap of £50,000 (coupled with a house price cap at £300,000) had almost no inflationary effect, and each £10,000 increase lead to proportionate price rises. It made little difference to house price inflation whether access was restricted to new homes or any homes on the open market."]},{"k":"p","s":["Interestingly, in our model, the new scheme did lead to lower local rents. With more renters able to access the mortgage market – a likely effect of the low 2.5% deposit requirement – demand for rental housing would decrease. In turn, landlords would lower rents or put homes up for sale, thus increasing the supply in the owner-occupier market."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Buying your first home? Here’s how to increase your chances of getting a mortgage","https://theconversation.com/buying-your-first-home-heres-how-to-increase-your-chances-of-getting-a-mortgage-224574"]]},{"k":"h","s":["An incomplete solution"]},{"k":"p","s":["The conclusion from our analysis is that there is no silver bullet for making housing more affordable, other than the long-term solution of building more homes to consistently increase supply."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the government genuinely wants to increase access to housing without further pricing people out of the market, income caps have to be considered carefully."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although Your First Home has an income cap, it is too high. It currently equates to the combined salaries of two people both earning near the top 10% of earners, and will not restrict access in any meaningful way."]},{"k":"p","s":["Short-term fixes, involving either subsidies for some sectors or increased taxes (for example on expensive housing), are extremely difficult to design without also causing unintended effects – not just for those buying and selling houses, but also for those who rent, since the rental and the purchase markets are so closely intertwined."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new scheme will undoubtedly allow some people to fulfil their dream of home ownership. But for many, it could exacerbate the housing crisis even further."]}],"chars":5512},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/maldives":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"f2e1b7a620249d121c3bda7e6f4b682193005afad3f5de532e9df42972ced574","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/maldives","bytes":63648,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Maldives travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-13T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-12T11:35:58+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to the situation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights. This may impact connections to and from the Maldives."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy to confirm what is covered"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media and sign up for FCDO travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hotline number Ministry of Tourism and Environment: +9609423131"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/maldives/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Maldives’ current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Maldives set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Maldivian High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least one month after the date you arrive in Maldives. ",["Make sure your passport is not damaged","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/replace"]," or you may be stopped by immigration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You will get a 30-day visa on arrival if you enter Maldives as a tourist."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you intend to work in Maldives, you must ",["get a work visa before you travel","https://www.immigration.gov.mv/work-visa/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information on entry requirements and visas, contact the Maldives immigration department."]},{"k":"h","s":["Traveller declaration form"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["complete a traveller declaration form (IMUGA)","https://imuga.immigration.gov.mv/traveller"]," within 96 hours before your flight arrives in the Maldives."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Maldives, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Maldives guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/139/maldives#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Maldives","https://www.maldiveshighcommission.uk/index.php/maldives/customs-information"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to bring in anything deemed contrary to Islam, including ‘idols for worship’, bibles, pork and pork products, and alcohol."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Maldives"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Maldives cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist groups, such as Al-Qaida and Daesh, have called on their supporters to carry out terrorist attacks in response to the conflict in Israel and Palestine. The conflict could also motivate individuals to carry out attacks, including in Maldives."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Maldivian authorities have disrupted a number of terrorist attack plans since 2017 and have made several arrests relating to attack planning, recruitment of terrorist fighters and spreading extremist ideology. However, a risk from terrorism remains."]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of attacks in the last 5 years include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2025, a terrorist plot was foiled. Suspects are awaiting trial."]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2022, a politician was attacked with a knife and injured in the Hulhumalé area of Malé"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2021, a high-profile politician and a number of bystanders were injured by the detonation of an improvised explosive device (IED) in central Malé"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2020, an arson attack on a police speedboat in Laamu Gan"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2020, knife attacks that injured 3 foreigners in Hulhumalé which were claimed by Daesh supporters"]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political protests take place occasionally in Malé. Avoid any protests or rallies to ensure your safety and security."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low in the exclusive resort islands, but petty crime does happen. Do not leave items unattended on the beach or in unlocked hotel rooms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Outside the resorts, there are incidents of gang-related violence including knife crime, mainly in Malé and in Hulhumalé. Avoid empty roads when on foot, particularly after dark."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Maldives is an Islamic country. It is illegal to publicly observe a religion other than Islam. Make sure that your actions do not offend, especially during Ramadan or when visiting religious areas around mosques. If you break local laws, you may get a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. In 2026, it began on 17 February and finished on 19 March. In 2027, it may start on 7 February and last for 29 or 30 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["During this time, do not eat, drink or smoke in public in the daytime, outside of holiday resorts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alcoholic drinks are only available on resort islands. Do not take any alcohol out of your resort. You can be arrested and deported for possessing and drinking alcohol, or being intoxicated outside resorts and on inhabited islands."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession, trafficking and manufacture of any illegal drugs are serious offences in Maldives and penalties can be severe. This includes cannabis, even small quantities can lead to arrest."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals have been caught carrying controlled drugs while transiting Maldives."]},{"k":"p","s":["International airports in Maldives have advanced scanning systems and procedures in place for scanning and detecting illegal substances, including cannabis. This includes all carry-on and checked-in baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Maldivian authorities have a zero-tolerance policy to drug offences. Possessing drugs, even in very small quantities, carries severe penalties, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["arrest and detention"]},{"k":"li","s":["long prison sentences if convicted"]},{"k":"li","s":["corporal punishment (whipping) in some cases"]},{"k":"li","s":["death penalty for the most serious offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["You are strongly advised:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not to carry any controlled substances, including cannabis, even if legal in your departure country"]},{"k":"li","s":["to check your luggage thoroughly before travelling or transiting through the Maldives"]},{"k":"li","s":["if prescribed medication contains controlled substances, carry a doctor’s prescription and check Maldivian regulations in advance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take tortoiseshell jewellery or ornaments, or pieces of coral out of Maldives."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relations are illegal and if you are convicted, you could get a fine or a lengthy prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Local dress standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should be sensitive to local dress standards when outside holiday resorts, including on beaches used by locals. Men and women should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have shoulders covered"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid short or tight-fitting shorts"]},{"k":"li","s":["have arms and upper legs covered when bathing"]},{"k":"p","s":["Nudism and topless sunbathing are not allowed anywhere, including on resort islands."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["The sea around Maldives can have strong tidal currents that can drag you away from the shoreline resulting in drownings. It is important that you know the risks and what you can do to minimise them. Always speak to the appropriate resort staff to find out where it is safe for you to swim."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should read the security information provided by your tour operator and make yourself aware of local swimming conditions on arrival at the resort. Keep in regular contact with resort staff to see if these conditions change."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only swim in well supervised areas, areas designated as safe for tourists, or where lifeguards are available. Pay attention to warning signs or flags and avoid swimming in areas with strong currents, high waves or dangerous underwater conditions. If something does not feel right, get out of the water at the earliest opportunity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Being aware of the potential dangers will help you to stay safe. Always take local advice before going into the sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been fatal accidents involving boat propellers in the South Ari Marine Protected Area (SAMPA) and nearby whale shark tourism sites. Regulations requiring propeller guards are not yet fully enforced. Take extra care when swimming or snorkelling near boats and follow local safety instructions."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday%22%20/t%20%22_blank"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many resort islands are more than an hour away from the nearest hyperbaric chamber. Make sure you understand how your dive operator would get you to one of the 3 chambers in the islands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Diving safaris are available and may include opportunities to see sharks. Be aware of the potential risks as accidents can occur and, in rare cases, may be fatal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive a car in Maldives, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience and minimum age 20 or 21."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk of piracy and armed robbery in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been attacks on local fishing sailing vessels (dhows) in the Gulf of Aden and Horn of Africa."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling by sea, read about the ",["regional risks at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most of the island resorts are accessible by boat. Pay attention to safety briefings when taking any boat trips. Make sure life jackets are provided, especially on smaller excursion boats. Some tour guides may be able to advise on the safety record and registration of boats."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flash flooding can affect low-lying islands during periods of heavy rain. Follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/extreme-weather-and-natural-hazards"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 102 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Maldives","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/139/maldives#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Maldives","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/139/maldives"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["measles"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Maldives"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities are limited – the only fully equipped hospitals are in Malé and Hulhumalé. Most resort islands are within reach of a doctor or have their own medical facilities, but many are several hours’ travel away from emergency treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Maldives","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/maldives-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Maldives","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-maldies"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Maldives"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 102"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 118"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 119"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=maldives"]," in Maldives"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Maldives","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/maldives-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Maldives","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/maldives-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/maldives/british-high-commission-male"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/maldives/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":14667,"change":"Updated information about swimming safety ( 'Safety and security’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sudan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"e54f605ea5ceb4f377e484bf4134763067efb809dece30247d0f2087b421bc47","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/sudan","bytes":76982,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Sudan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-07T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-05-11T16:07:13+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Sudan because of the ongoing military conflict in Khartoum and other parts of the country. This does not include the Hala’ib Triangle and the Bir Tawil Trapezoid where FCDO advises against all but essential travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several ceasefires, but these have been regularly broken."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor travel advice and other media reports for the latest information."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sudan/safety-and-security"]," in Sudan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get help in Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy in Khartoum is closed due to the conflict. There are no British consular staff in Sudan. Our ability to provide consular support is severely limited and we cannot provide in-person support inside Sudan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British national in Sudan, you can call our 24/7 telephone helpline: +44 1908 516 666. Select option 2 for consular services for British nationals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Leaving Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK government is no longer evacuating people from Sudan."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO cannot offer advice on the safety of travelling to any potential departure point. Consider carefully whether you want to take any of the available options."]},{"k":"p","s":["Use your own judgement to move towards a departure point if and when you judge it is safe to do so."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK government’s ability to facilitate onward travel from countries in the region is limited and you’ll be expected to cover the cost of visas, accommodation, insurance and onward travel yourself."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any travel options you pursue are taken at your own risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO cannot help non-British dependants of British nationals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel against FCDO advice, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sudan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK who choose to travel against FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Sudan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Sudan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Sudanese Embassy in the UK","https://www.sudanembassy.org.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Sudan, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Sudan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["apply for a visa through the Sudanese Embassy in the UK","https://www.sudanembassy.org.uk/visa-service/"],", or through the Sudanese embassy in the country you’re travelling from."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Exit visas"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter Sudan on a single-entry visa, you’ll need an exit visa to leave the country, though this is not always enforced. You can get more information on exit visas from Port Sudan Airport Immigration. You may need to show proof of your sponsor and pay the exit visa fee."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["You will not be allowed to leave the Red Sea State without a travel permit. You need to apply for that once in country and pay a fee. The requirements for each state are different. You will have to pay different amounts and go through different processes depending on your destination."]},{"k":"h","s":["Previous travel to Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If your passport has an Israeli visa, entry or exit stamp, you will not be allowed to enter Sudan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Sudan, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Sudan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/212/sudan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must register with the Aliens Department at the Ministry of Interior within 3 days of your arrival in Sudan. You will need 2 passport size photos and to pay a fee."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not register within 3 days of arrival, you may be fined. Some larger hotels will do this for you. Ask when you check-in."]},{"k":"h","s":["Children and young people"]},{"k":"p","s":["As well as a visa, children aged 17 and under must have their father’s consent to enter and exit Sudan. Children travelling without their father need a letter giving consent for them to enter and exit Sudan, though this is not always enforced."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get the letter stamped at the Sudanese Embassy in the UK before travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the father is absent, mothers or guardians must get a court order which shows they have sole custodial rights for the children."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the parents are divorced, you’ll need to show divorce documents."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the father has died, you’ll need to show the death certificate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the ",["Sudanese Embassy in the UK","https://www.sudanembassy.org.uk/"]," for more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Sudan. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Sudan","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sudan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorism attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreigners, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["major gatherings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Red Sea military activity"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a military response to Houthi militants’ attempts to disrupt international shipping in the Red Sea. The military activity is limited to the Red Sea and Yemen, but travel advice for nearby countries could change at short notice. You should monitor travel advice and follow instructions from local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Security situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an ongoing conflict across Sudan following violent clashes, which started in April 2023."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been widespread violent crime in Khartoum since the start of the conflict. There have also been reports of a large increase in crime in other cities and areas of Sudan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Types of crime include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["looting"]},{"k":"li","s":["burglaries and home invasions"]},{"k":"li","s":["theft"]},{"k":"li","s":["muggings"]},{"k":"li","s":["demands for money at checkpoints"]},{"k":"li","s":["mobile phone and bag-snatching, including drive-by bag-snatching by thieves on motorbikes"]},{"k":"li","s":["aggressive begging, including attempts to open the doors of stopped vehicles"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce the risk to yourself and your belongings, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not leave valuable items on display"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep doors locked and windows closed when driving"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re stopped or attacked, comply with demands and do not resist."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of detention, including kidnap, enforced disappearances and unlawful arrest across Sudan. There have been a number of recent incidents where British nationals and other westerners have been detained against their will."]},{"k":"p","s":["Humanitarian aid workers and journalists are viewed as legitimate targets."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mobile phone and internet access"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular communication blackouts. Mobile phone and internet services are not always available. Telecommunications networks could be disrupted without warning."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is a legal requirement to carry photographic ID, such as a passport, with you at all times."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Non-Muslim women do not have to wear a veil or cover their heads. Men and women should dress modestly and respect local customs and sensitivities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sudan is an Islamic country. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions. Make sure your actions do not cause offence, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or if you intend to visit religious areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol and drug laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Non-Muslims are allowed to drink alcohol in Sudan, but not in the presence of Muslims. However, you may still be arrested for drinking alcohol regardless of the circumstances."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for drug trafficking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the conflict, it is not advisable to take photographs in secure areas in Sudan. Do not take photographs or use a mobile phone camera close to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["military installations"]},{"k":"li","s":["public utilities, including petrol stations"]},{"k":"li","s":["other sensitive areas, such as bridges and airports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Plain-clothed public security officers operate in these areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Sudan and not tolerated in Sudanese society. This includes inviting guests into hotel rooms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Relationships outside marriage"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to have extramarital relations and there are severe penalties. It’s illegal to live together, or to share the same hotel room, with someone of the opposite sex if you’re not married or closely related."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Guests in hotel rooms"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to invite guests into your hotel room. Business meetings should take place in hotel lobbies or meeting rooms, not hotel rooms. Tourist police patrol the hotels, and British nationals have reported problems with Sudanese authorities about this."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Technical equipment"]},{"k":"p","s":["You might need a licence to use some technical equipment in Sudan, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["satellite phones"]},{"k":"li","s":["listening or recording devices"]},{"k":"li","s":["radio transmitters"]},{"k":"li","s":["powerful cameras or binoculars"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the ",["Sudanese Embassy in the UK","https://www.sudanembassy.org.uk/"]," before travelling for more information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s difficult to use non-Sudanese credit or debit cards, and most banks and ATM machines will not let you withdraw cash. Bring US dollars with you to Sudan."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be able to exchange US dollars dated 2006 onwards (older ones will not be exchanged), but this will be difficult due to the current conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["British pounds are rarely exchanged. Only change money through banks or official exchange bureaus."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Sudan, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Sudan for up to 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions and safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road travel will involve heightened levels of risk due to the current conflict and should only be undertaken if strictly necessary."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions are poor. Roads, even major ones, might:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be untarred or unsurfaced"]},{"k":"li","s":["have potholes"]},{"k":"li","s":["be used by pedestrians, donkey-carts and rickshaws"]},{"k":"p","s":["At night, there is generally no street lighting and many vehicles do not have lights. Many drivers in Sudan do not have a licence or insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road traffic accidents are common. There is a high risk of traffic accidents when using public transport or vehicles for hire, such as rickshaws and ‘amjad minivans’."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sudanese law prohibits the use of mobile phones while driving."]},{"k":"h","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Khartoum Airport and Port Sudan Airport are operating limited numbers of international and domestic flights. However, both airports have been the target of drone strikes due to the ongoing conflict. The risk of further attacks continues and might cause the airports to close on a temporary basis again."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no Sudanese airlines which currently meet the standards required to operate direct flights to the UK or EU."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list#sudan"]," (ASL) lists all known airlines in Sudan that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a significant risk of ",["piracy in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],". The threat assessment of the combined international naval counter-piracy forces is that sailing yachts should not enter the ",["designated high-risk area","https://on-shore.mschoa.org/"],", due to the risk of hijacking."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you go ashore along the Red Sea coast, make sure you have reviewed the relevant country travel advice and have the correct documentation for entry."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rainy season"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flash flooding can happen during the rainy season from July to October. Risks at this time of year include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["flooding that can make areas inaccessible by road, including areas south of Khartoum"]},{"k":"li","s":["dry riverbeds (‘wadis’) being hit by flash floods, with many only being passable on a major road"]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has extra safety advice for regions of Sudan. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sudan"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sudan/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling to Saudi Arabia from Port Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["For information about arriving in Jeddah and entry requirements, see ",["Saudi Arabia travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re arriving in Jeddah from Port Sudan and need urgent assistance, you can contact FCDO in Jeddah on +966 (0)12 622 5550 and select option 4."]},{"k":"h","s":["Leaving Sudan by a land border"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re considering leaving Sudan across a land border, check that the border crossing will be open."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sudan’s borders with ",["Chad","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chad"]," and ",["Eritrea","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea"]," are currently closed."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Check the travel advice for the country you will be entering","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," to understand the entry requirements for that country and whether FCDO advises against travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sudan-Egypt border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Significant numbers of people are trying to cross the border from Sudan into Egypt. There are 2 main land border crossings between Egypt and Sudan, at Argeen and Qustul. The nearest town in Sudan to the crossings is Wadi Halfa, 30km from border."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is almost no infrastructure at these border crossings. People are waiting several days to cross the border, with limited access to food and water."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy in Egypt does not have staff at the border. Our ability to provide help is very limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British national planning to cross into Egypt at Argeen or Qustul and you do not have valid documentation with you, call the British Embassy in Cairo: + 20 (0) 2 2791 6000."]},{"k":"p","s":["See our ",["Egypt travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt"]," for entry requirements, including information on visas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["The current conflict has severely affected health services and many may be unavailable, including ",["hospitals for British nationals in Khartoum","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/sudan-list-of-medical-facilities/list-of-hospitals-for-british-nationals-in-khartoum"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in the country are limited and medical evacuation is likely to be necessary for all but the most basic treatments. Make sure you have ",["adequate travel and medical insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a particular risk to public health in areas of conflict where immunisation coverage is poor."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency services in Sudan have been severely impacted by the conflict and are often unresponsive."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need emergency medical treatment you should make your own way to hospital, if you can."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Sudan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/212/sudan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Sudan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/212/sudan"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["cholera"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro has more information on ",["malaria in Sudan","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/212/sudan#Malaria"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Other health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular outbreaks of chikungunya, dengue, measles and other diseases in Sudan, particularly in refugee camps. There is a lack of clean water and the inability to remove dead bodies means Sudan is at high risk from various diseases."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency services in Sudan have been severely impacted by the conflict and are often unresponsive."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=sudan"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Sudan"]," in Sudan"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Sudan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/sudan-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Sudan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/sudan-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/sudan/british-embassy-khartoum"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sudan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":18641,"change":"Updated information on operations in Sudanese airports ('Safety and security' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/yes-men-and-boys-should-be-shamed-for-misogyny-its-part-of-how-we-stamp-it-out-296485":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T03:47Z","sha":"9f6f5da963f84ab22f9fcbc4e4d47fab7ce9b72a7d4d4a9c431c0a72e05bf4cd","read":"https://theconversation.com/yes-men-and-boys-should-be-shamed-for-misogyny-its-part-of-how-we-stamp-it-out-296485","bytes":180634,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Yes, men and boys should be shamed for misogyny. It’s part of how we stamp it out","by":[{"n":"Steven Roberts","r":"Professor of Sociology, School of Social Sciences, Monash University"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T03:21:12Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The headlines of recent weeks and months have been dominated by men accused of doing terrible things to women."]},{"k":"p","s":["Russell Brand has ",["been jailed","https://theconversation.com/justice-accountability-more-questions-what-russell-brands-guilty-verdict-means-for-victim-survivors-296042"]," for historical crimes of rape and sexual assault, and now David Walliams is under ",["police investigation","https://www.smh.com.au/culture/celebrity/police-investigating-children-s-author-and-little-britain-star-david-walliams-for-sex-offences-20261114-p61e3l.html"]," for allegations about his ",["grooming and predatory behaviour","https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/ng-interactive/2026/nov/10/david-walliams-accused-sex-grooming-allegations-young-women"]," towards teenage girls (allegations he denies)."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s significant that these historical cases are coming to public attention now. They represent a form of legal accountability that has taken years to arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["But we should not mistake justice finally catching up with some prominent men for evidence the culture has caught up too. The behaviours and attitudes these cases expose are hardly confined to the past."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent cases, including the ",["Cornell Seven","https://theconversation.com/the-cornell-7-reported-rape-shows-why-we-need-to-rethink-sexual-violence-prevention-293338"]," in the United States, remind us these are not simply historical problems. They point to the continuing challenges of sexual violence and entitlement."]},{"k":"p","s":["All of this occurs against the backdrop of an increasingly noisy debate about boys and young men being “ ",["in crisis","https://www.abc.net.au/religion/senator-matt-canavan-blaming-feminism-for-the-manosphere/107118108"],"”. Some ",["warn","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-13/manosphere-masculinity-questions-answered-live-blog/107216354"]," ",["against","https://www.spectator.com.au/2024/05/winning-over-young-men/"]," “shaming” men and boys as we hold them to account for poor treatment of women."]},{"k":"p","s":["But shame can be constructive. And our current cultural moment shows us why it’s needed."]},{"k":"h","s":["A misogynistic world"]},{"k":"p","s":["These are all different cases with different circumstances. While Brand has been convicted and sentenced, no charges have been laid against Walliams so far."]},{"k":"p","s":["But all these instances reinforce that there is still considerable work to do to protect women."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s not just at the level of culturally celebrated men. The misogynistic attitudes that underpin these acts of harm remain present in our ",["schools","https://bridges.monash.edu/articles/report/Duty_of_Care_Teachers_experiences_of_sexism_misogyny_and_sexual_harassment_in_Australian_schools/32942816"],", ",["workplaces","https://www.ourwatch.org.au/news/sexual-harassment-response-a-key-issue-in-attracting-and-retaining-staff-new-data-shows"],", ",["sporting organisations","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/gwao.70214"]," and wider society."]},{"k":"p","s":["Misogyny is also ",["the common thread","https://theconversation.com/we-may-be-able-to-turn-off-the-algorithm-but-we-cant-escape-the-misogyny-of-the-manosphere-291552"]," throughout the disparate content in the manosphere, which itself has been the focus of much media coverage this year."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Research has shown","https://doi.org/10.64628/AA.3uw996gda"]," misogyny can also be the clearest warning sign of future violent extremism. It can’t be dismissed as merely rhetoric: misogyny poses a real risk to the safety of women and girls."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["You’d better start paying attention to the manosphere. You’re living in it","https://theconversation.com/youd-better-start-paying-attention-to-the-manosphere-youre-living-in-it-279547"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Walking on eggshells"]},{"k":"p","s":["Feminist organisations and those working to prevent men’s violence are routinely warned, particularly by boys’ and men’s advocacy organisations, ",["not to shame boys or make them","https://aapnews.aap.com.au/news/rewrite-rules-to-protect-kids-violence-inquiry-told"]," feel like future perpetrators of violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["This has become a ",["common warning","https://www.mamamia.com.au/parenting-boys-manosphere/"],": violence prevention work must be careful about how it engages boys, so as not to alienate them."]},{"k":"p","s":["These warnings distract from the substance of gender violence prevention work. Attention shifts away from the behaviours and attitudes that need to change and towards the supposed harm caused by asking boys to confront them."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a striking irony here. We seem increasingly concerned about boys being shamed for something they have not done, while remaining far less concerned with making the behaviours that actually harm women and girls shameful."]},{"k":"h","s":["Shame on who?"]},{"k":"p","s":["A big part of the problem is how we understand shame. We have become accustomed to thinking of it primarily as an attack on someone’s confidence or sense of self that can provoke defensiveness and even aggression."]},{"k":"p","s":["But this is only one way shame operates. Shame can also have a generative ",["social and cultural function","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1111/0735-2751.00089"],". It can reinforce shared expectations, establish boundaries and ",["signal that certain behaviours are unacceptable","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35797281/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The mistake is to treat these different functions as though they are the same."]},{"k":"p","s":["We should not humiliate boys, make them feel ashamed of who they are or suggest they are destined to perpetrate violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["But we should want them to recognise that misogyny, sexual entitlement and the abuse of power are shameful."]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the conviction of her ex-husband and 47 other men for raping her, Gisèle Pelicot ",["said","https://www.bbc.com/audio/play/w3ct71d9"]," “shame must change sides”."]},{"k":"p","s":["This offers a powerful reminder of where shame belongs. It should not belong to women who experience sexual violence, or those who speak about it. It belongs with those who perpetrate it."]},{"k":"p","s":["But making shame change sides requires more than condemning individual acts of sexual violence. It means confronting the masculine norms of dominance and control that enable, excuse and normalise these behaviours."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tackling the real problem"]},{"k":"p","s":["We need to be honest with boys about this. Teaching boys to recognise and resist these expectations is not blaming them for men’s violence. It’s inviting them to question and reject norms that underpin harms to ",["boys themselves","https://theconversation.com/dont-blame-toxic-masculinity-for-online-misogyny-the-manosphere-is-hurting-men-too-254802"],", as well as the women, girls and gender diverse people they interact with."]},{"k":"p","s":["When ",["commentators","https://www.spectator.com.au/2024/05/winning-over-young-men/"]," and boys’ and men’s advocacy organisations frame this education as in any way shaming boys, they ",["construct a grievance narrative","https://womensagenda.com.au/latest/how-the-discourse-on-boys-alienation-is-fuelled-by-anti-feminist-agendas/"]," in which boys are portrayed as under attack. The challenge to harmful masculine norms is then situated as the problem, rather than the norms themselves."]},{"k":"p","s":["Boys learn about gender and relationships from families, schools, friends, media and institutions, including from what adults choose to challenge or ignore. That was true in the early 2000s, when prominent men could enjoy celebrity and public admiration despite cultures of misogyny and sexual entitlement."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is true now, as the cases currently in the public eye remind us."]},{"k":"p","s":["We should want boys to recognise these behaviours, and the cultures that sustain them, as shameful. Our responsibility is to give them the understanding, confidence and critical tools to reach that conclusion for themselves."]}],"chars":5415},"https://theconversation.com/expect-to-see-fewer-and-smaller-potatoes-this-christmas-its-the-worst-harvest-since-1950s-295934":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T17:08Z","sha":"685aad0818d6bd9db0162d6c62cfeca91052cdd69d01f46adb04236827731f0f","read":"https://theconversation.com/expect-to-see-fewer-and-smaller-potatoes-this-christmas-its-the-worst-harvest-since-1950s-295934","bytes":181844,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Expect to see fewer and smaller potatoes this Christmas – it’s the ‘worst harvest since 1950s’","by":[{"n":"Robin Gowers","r":"Senior Lecturer at the Writtle School of Agriculture, Animal and Environmental Sciences, Anglia Ruskin University"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T15:46:10Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Britain’s potato harvest this winter could be one of the smallest in decades."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is partly down to the hot summer and a poor growing year. Potatoes have shallow roots and ",["need steady moisture","https://www.potatonewstoday.com/2026/08/12/englands-drought-deepens-as-potato-growers-confront-mounting-yield-and-quality-risks/"],", so dry spells cut yield and size. Where ",["farmers","https://theconversation.com/uk/search?q=farming"]," had stored water to regularly irrigate, crops fared better."]},{"k":"p","s":["With ",["75% of England","https://www.bbc.co.uk/weather/articles/cqvgy1lejp7ro"]," in drought in September, and ",["Wales","https://www.gov.wales/written-statement-update-dry-weather-drought-and-water-resources-wales"]," also affected by dry conditions, one model estimated that British potato yields would be 11% below average. It used ",["the 2018 harvest as a guide","https://www.fpcfreshtalkdaily.co.uk/post/british-potato-growers-face-losses-of-up-to-169m-after-summer-drought"],". Some farmers reported a greater than ",["50% drop","https://www.fsfruit.co.uk/potato-update-13-august-2026/"]," in how many potatoes they were harvesting."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wholesale prices had already risen by more than ",["40% by early August","https://www.grocerygazette.co.uk/2026/08/04/uk-potato-crop-faces-heatwave-squeeze-as-wholesale-prices-surge-40/"],". By September, big British buyers were reportedly ",["paying more than £300 a tonne","https://hortnews.com/british-potato-growers-face-losses-of-up-to-169m/"]," for potatoes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Food and Drink Federation has warned of the ",["worst potato harvest since the 1950s","https://www.potatonewstoday.com/2026/10/16/britains-potato-harvest-under-pressure-as-industry-warns-of-smallest-crop-in-decades/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Growers have warned supermarkets to expect smaller potatoes and tighter supplies this year, so shoppers may need to accept wider variation in ",["size and quality","https://www.potatonewstoday.com/2026/08/12/englands-drought-deepens-as-potato-growers-confront-mounting-yield-and-quality-risks/"],". This is partly because other ",["European countries","https://www.fpcfreshtalkdaily.co.uk/post/british-potato-growers-face-losses-of-up-to-169m-after-summer-drought"],", which often provide supplies to the UK, suffered the same hot summer, and this affected their crops, too."]},{"k":"p","s":["But shoppers may not feel the full effect of higher wholesale prices this winter. Potatoes are more likely to become significantly more expensive next year. It is also worth noting that ",["many supermarkets","https://www.potatopro.com/news/2023/farmers-outraged-sainsbury%E2%80%99s-sells-potatoes-less-cost-production"]," subsidise potato prices."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Lidl has announced","https://www.thegrocer.co.uk/news/lidl-fires-starting-gun-on-2026-christmas-dinner-wars/725648.article"]," that a 2kg bag will ",["cost 9p","https://www.walesonline.co.uk/news/uk-news/lidl-confirms-exact-date-cut-34922687"]," in the week before Christmas. The supermarket says it is funding the low price itself, so this price tells shoppers nothing about what the crop costs to grow."]},{"k":"p","s":["Supermarkets agree prices and volumes with farmers ",["well in advance","https://www.fsfruit.co.uk/potato-update-13-august-2026/"],". Retailers ",["may absorb","https://www.grocerygazette.co.uk/2026/08/04/uk-potato-crop-faces-heatwave-squeeze-as-wholesale-prices-surge-40/"]," some of the higher costs this year rather than risk losing customers to competitors."]},{"k":"p","s":["The bigger question is whether British farmers will carry on planting Britain’s ",["favourite vegetable","https://yougov.com/en-gb/ratings/vegetables"]," in future, and what happens if more decide it is no longer worth the risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2025, the issue was too many potatoes heading for shops – the UK produced ",["5.5 million tonnes","https://www.grocerygazette.co.uk/2026/08/04/uk-potato-crop-faces-heatwave-squeeze-as-wholesale-prices-surge-40/"],", 8.5% more than the year before. This caused prices paid to farmers to collapse."]},{"k":"p","s":["By February 2026, top-quality maris piper potatoes were ",["fetching about £180 a tonne","https://www.freshplaza.com/europe/article/9809073/uk-potato-prices-fall-as-surplus-weighs-on-2026-outlook/"]," on the open market, less than half the £400 of a year earlier. Contract prices for the following year were also ",["weaker","https://www.farminguk.com/news/potato-growers-face-viability-test-as-costs-and-contract-prices-bite_68566.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Growers did what economics predicts: they planted less. Analysts put this year’s area in Great Britain at around ",["101,000 hectares","https://ca1-eci.edcdn.com/Potato-harvests-analysis-140926.pdf?v=1789485025"],", well below the ",["117,500 recorded in 2020","https://horticulture.ahdb.org.uk/potato/production"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then came the heat and drought."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why can’t farmers cash in?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Higher prices should encourage farmers to plant more. But a price spike helps only those with potatoes to sell at open-market rates. Most crops are grown under contract, and growers who struggle to deliver the agreed tonnage or quality ",["may miss out","https://www.potatonewstoday.com/2026/08/12/englands-drought-deepens-as-potato-growers-confront-mounting-yield-and-quality-risks/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some big buyers that normally rely on contracts are buying open-market potatoes as fast as they can, so growers with uncommitted crops ",["may do well","https://www.fsfruit.co.uk/potato-update-13-august-2026/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, costs for farmers keep climbing. Conflict in the Middle East has pushed up ",["energy and fertiliser costs","https://theconversation.com/fertiliser-the-forgotten-history-linking-the-agricultural-commodity-and-empire-in-wartime-283114"],". Labour and machinery are also more expensive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, the end of the ",["basic payment scheme","https://uk.practicallaw.thomsonreuters.com/0-586-7265?transitionType=Default&contextData=(sc.Default)&firstPage=true"]," (an annual payment for farmers that followed environmental guidelines) and ",["controversies","https://nationalpigassociation.co.uk/defra-accused-of-cruellest-betrayal-yet-after-sudden-closure-of-sfi-applications/"]," about its replacements may have removed a financial cushion that once helped farms through bad years."]},{"k":"p","s":["The potato contract price is fixed in advance, so growers have little room to pass costs on. Tighter margins are also hitting buyers, packers and processors, but it is growers that carry the bulk of the weather risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Economists call this pattern ",["the cobweb cycle","https://www.economicshelp.org/blog/glossary/cobweb-theory/"],". In the textbook version, farmers plant according to last season’s price, so a glut leads to a price crash, then cuts in planting, then shortage and high prices, then over-planting again. Potatoes have followed this familiar cycle almost to the letter this year."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet several forces pull the other way. Speaking before the summer’s hot weather and drought, in May, Scott Walker, chief executive of the industry body representing the potato sector, GB Potatoes, said that many growers were weighing up how much exposure they would ",["carry into 2027","https://www.farminguk.com/news/potato-growers-face-viability-test-as-costs-and-contract-prices-bite_68566.html"],". The body has warned that growers could leave the business or reduce their crop."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contract prices were weaker this year, costs are higher, and drought has shown how exposed the crop is. Depressed cereal markets offer little alternative income, so a wholesale exit is not certain either."]},{"k":"p","s":["Farmers will be looking closely at what supermarkets offer them in 2027. High open market prices alone will not bring growers back."]},{"k":"p","s":["Two things matter most: the contracts offered this winter, and whether farmers can secure water supplies for next summer. Signs are that water access may remain tight. For instance, the Environment Agency put England’s reservoirs at only ",["54% of capacity in early October","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/dry-weather-and-drought-in-england-2026-summary-reports/dry-weather-and-drought-in-england-2-to-8-october-2026"],". Higher prices could prompt a rebound in planting, but a normal-weather harvest could tip the market back into glut, forcing prices down again."]},{"k":"h","s":["Will British farmers stop planting potatoes?"]},{"k":"p","s":["In September 2026, the Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs saw no indication that winter ",["supplies were at risk","https://www.potatonewstoday.com/2026/10/16/britains-potato-harvest-under-pressure-as-industry-warns-of-smallest-crop-in-decades/"]," but added that it was too early to assess the drought’s full impact on potato production and that there was, at that point, no indication that winter potato supplies were at risk. Registered potato farmer numbers fell from about ",["2,466 in 2000 to 1,611 in 2020","https://hortnews.com/number-potato-growers-continues-reduce/"],", when the statutory body collating data on potato farmers was discontinued. But each bad year pushes more to ask whether the crop is worth it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tim Rooke, National Farmers’ Union potato policy group chair, said in 2025 that ",["the UK imports","https://www.fwi.co.uk/business/markets-and-trends/crop-prices/hort-and-potato-growers-discuss-rising-costs-with-minister"]," approximately 1 million tonnes of frozen chips a year, because the risk against return on investment of growing potatoes is astronomically high."]},{"k":"p","s":["A food system that leaves a shrinking number of growers to absorb the weather and price risk should not be surprised when they plant less. One option could be fairer contracts that share risk, and investment in water storage. But less certain supply chains and more volatile prices could cost shoppers more."]},{"k":"p","s":["Climate change means ",["water shortages","https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/research/climate/understanding-climate/uk-and-global-extreme-events-drought"]," and high temperatures will happen more often across Europe. Potato farmers ",["are, therefore, likely to face these challenges","https://ca1-eci.edcdn.com/Potato-harvests-analysis-140926.pdf?v=1789485025"]," more regularly in the future."]}],"chars":6271},"https://theconversation.com/history-shows-canadas-attempts-to-exploit-arctic-oil-have-failed-296584":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T18:22Z","sha":"c25e3a2ce3e14e9f00b90e31fc988e467162add4eca9e8f65a780835e6d8c472","read":"https://theconversation.com/history-shows-canadas-attempts-to-exploit-arctic-oil-have-failed-296584","bytes":183504,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"History shows Canada’s attempts to exploit Arctic oil have failed","by":[{"n":"Jonathan Peyton","r":"Associate Professor in Environment and Geography and Associate Dean (Academic) CHRFEER, University of Manitoba"},{"n":"Warren Bernauer","r":"Assistant Professor, Department of Environment & Geography, University of Manitoba"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T17:15:58Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Liberal members of Parliament in Canada recently ",["agreed to amend","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/bill-c-39-major-projects-fast-track-environmental-concerns-amendments-9.7424528"]," the controversial proposed legislation, ",["Bill C-39","https://theconversation.com/what-bill-c-39s-loosened-environmental-regulations-could-mean-for-canadians-294851"],", that critics say would undermine environmental protections and Indigenous and labour rights if passed into law."]},{"k":"p","s":["The amendments come days after ",["protests against the bill","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/thunder-bay/bill-c39-rally-thunder-bay-9.7419849"]," took place in cities across Canada. The proposed legislation, called the Building Canada Strong Act, aims to fast-track development projects such as pipelines and mines."]},{"k":"p","s":["In line with that push, the Canadian government recently turned its attention to reviving interest in Arctic offshore oil and gas. ",["The fall 2026 budget","https://theconversation.com/budget-2026-gives-households-a-boost-but-businesses-get-the-biggest-break-295949"]," earmarked millions of dollars ",["for northern oil and gas governance","https://www.cbc.ca/player/play/video/9.7417380"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prime Minister Mark Carney has announced plans for consultations and capacity-building in the western Arctic, with an eye toward lifting a federal moratorium on ",["offshore oil and gas extraction in the Canadian Arctic","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/arctic-drilling-consultation-mark-carney-canada-9.7416538"],". But will this surge of political support lead to hydrocarbon production in the region?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Arctic oil and gas moratorium"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2016, the Canadian and American governments implemented a ",["moratorium on Arctic drilling","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/statements/2016/12/20/united-states-canada-joint-arctic-leaders-statement"],". The ban was meant to support climate commitments, ",["study the environmental risks","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/north/prime-minister-justin-trudeau-yellowknife-1.3975229"]," and develop parks and protected areas in line with international ",["commitments to preserve lands and waters","https://www.canada.ca/en/services/environment/conservation/conserving-30-by-2030.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ban’s ultimate promise was to build a ",["sustainable Arctic economy","https://nunatsiaq.com/stories/article/65674trudeau_bans_future_oil_gas_activity_in_canadian_arctic/"],", in partnership with other Arctic nations. But its reception in the North was mixed. Concern about missed potential ",["economic opportunities","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/northern-premiers-accuse-pm-of-failing-to-consult-on-drilling-issue-1.4271761"]," came with concern from others that the ",["ban didn’t go far enough","https://www.aptnnews.ca/national-news/trudeau-promises-ban-on-oil-drilling-in-the-arctic-but-what-about-seismic-testing/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bill C-39 has been criticized for the potential limits it would place on environmental protections, Indigenous and labour rights in the name of “ ",["building Canada strong","https://www.canada.ca/en/privy-council/campaigns/speech-throne/2025/building-canada-strong.html"],".” Arctic oil and gas opportunities appear to be one of the target resources of this policy."]},{"k":"p","s":["The history of Arctic offshore oil and gas extraction in Canada can tell us a lot about how these proposals might take shape in the present and future. The history of Canada’s attempt to build an oil and gas economy in Arctic waters is, for the most part, a history of failed projects."]},{"k":"h","s":["Expensive, complex and risky"]},{"k":"p","s":["Why did Arctic oil and gas projects fail? The most obvious answer is a combination of climate, geography and the risks these projects produce. In short, it is hugely expensive, technically complex and ecologically risky to move oil and gas from Arctic waters to southern refineries and markets. Uncertainty around jurisdiction and local community benefits further complicates the question of ",["Arctic oil and gas","https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009110044"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["On a broader scale, interest in offshore hydrocarbon resources in Arctic Canada tends to wax and wane alongside shifting geopolitical tensions and instabilities in oil-producing regions globally. ",["The Berger Inquiry","https://publications.gc.ca/collections/collection_2015/bcp-pco/CP32-25-1977-1-eng.pdf"]," into the Mackenzie Valley pipeline unfolded in the shadow of the 1973 oil embargo and Arab-Israeli War."]},{"k":"p","s":["The 1979 Iranian Revolution and oil shocks reinvigorated pressure for Arctic oil and gas production, with several Canadian and international energy companies submitting proposals for offshore production in ",["the Beaufort Sea","https://publications.gc.ca/collections/collection_2017/acee-ceaa/En105-30-1984-eng.pdf"],". A revived proposal for a ",["natural gas pipeline in the Mackenzie Valley","https://reviewboard.ca/registry/eir0405-001"]," was assessed in the context of surging energy prices tied to the 2003 invasion of Iraq by the United States."]},{"k":"p","s":["In each case, global prices for oil and gas dropped before the proposed projects began, rendering production commercially unviable."]},{"k":"h","s":["Science fiction infrastructure dreams"]},{"k":"p","s":["This geopolitical intrigue has made Arctic offshore oil and gas into a “stranded resource” — it’s easy to see the appeal of an untapped reserve."]},{"k":"p","s":["To solve the Arctic oil and gas riddle, engineers and oil executives have dreamed up a dizzying array of technological adaptations and infrastructures to move oil and gas to southern markets."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drill rigs on ",["floating ice islands of sand","https://doi.org/10.1016/0165-232X(83)90065-4"]," dredged from the ocean floor. Oil tankers split in half and towed into the Beaufort Sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["A type of 12-propeller plane, nicknamed the ",["Brute Lifter","https://www.teachingarcticenvironments.com/seriesone/boeing-rc1-the-brute-lifter"],", ferrying oil to Edmonton in the fuselage. ",["Nuclear submarines","https://doi.org/10.1016/0165-232X(83)90073-3"]," full of oil sailing under the ice. ",["Arctic island-hopping gas pipelines","https://doi.org/10.1080/10455752.2022.2141285"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["These and more science-fictional infrastructure dreams were all in the mix at one point or another. Similar ideas will have to be brought into being if the Canadian government proceeds with further exploration of Arctic oil and gas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Arctic resources as crisis response"]},{"k":"p","s":["The current push has many of the hallmarks of previous attempts to drill in Arctic waters. Carney’s interest in lifting the federal moratorium on offshore oil and gas extraction similarly responds to geopolitical instability and proposes huge, “dreamy” infrastructure investment."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this case, the Russian invasion of Ukraine and the U.S.-Israeli war against Iran are driving Canadian politicians to once again look to Arctic hydrocarbons as a ",["crisis response","https://utppublishing.com/doi/pdf/10.3138/jcs-2026-0005"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Projects of “ ",["national interest","https://www.canada.ca/en/one-canadian-economy/services/building-canada-act-projects-national-interest.html"],"” — such as an invigorated oil and gas economy in the western Arctic and Beaufort Sea or the ",["Port of Churchill Plus","https://www.canada.ca/en/privy-council/major-projects-office/projects/other/referred/churchill-plus.html"]," in northern Manitoba — are likely to gain traction. Time, money and work will be invested into consultations and assessments, including significant resources and labour from Indigenous organizations and communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The issue will likely once again prove divisive within and between Indigenous communities and organizations, leading to political conflict over proposed exploration and extraction activities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The end result is likely to be the same as previous attempts to extract oil and gas from Arctic waters in Canada. Projects will face the usual insurmountable economic, environmental and political barriers to development, and interest in Arctic oil and gas will once again wane."]},{"k":"p","s":["The last well drilled in the Beaufort Sea was in 2006. It remains to be seen if the Carney government can surmount the social, environmental and geopolitical barriers that led to previous failures to build an oil and gas economy in Canada’s Arctic."]}],"chars":5885},"https://theconversation.com/oil-100-years-ago-upton-sinclair-wrote-the-great-american-anti-capitalist-epic-277491":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T20:25Z","sha":"164fdf24db0b20ce2fac27aa9edd611f2ffe46c159a882ac50e66532a4f84001","read":"https://theconversation.com/oil-100-years-ago-upton-sinclair-wrote-the-great-american-anti-capitalist-epic-277491","bytes":199284,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Oil! – 100 years ago, Upton Sinclair wrote the great American anti-capitalist epic","by":[{"n":"Tamlyn Avery","r":"Senior Lecturer in English Literature, Adelaide University"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T19:11:48Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["First serialised in the Communist Party publication ",["The Daily Worker","https://www.marxists.org/history/usa/pubs/dailyworker/index.htm"]," in 1926–7, Upton Sinclair’s ",["Oil!","https://www.penguin.com.au/books/oil-9780143137443"]," is now known as the inspiration for Paul Thomas Anderson’s loose film adaptation ",["There Will Be Blood","https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0469494/"]," (2007). But the novel is one of American literature’s most prescient anti-capitalist epics."]},{"k":"p","s":["Set against the backdrop of California’s oil boom in the 1910s and the United States’ entry into the World War I, Oil! is a family saga that identifies the dark shadow looming behind almost all of modernity’s uneven developments and pressing social issues. The oil industry is to Sinclair’s socialist worldview what whaling is to Herman Melville’s ",["Moby-Dick","https://theconversation.com/guide-to-the-classics-moby-dick-by-herman-melville-52000"],". Whether ",["spermaceti","https://www.britannica.com/topic/spermaceti"]," or crude, oil makes legible the entire incomprehensible sweep of the modern world as we know it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sinclair sets out to prove that oil is not an inert substance; it is the all-too-real lubricant that keeps the cogs of capitalism turning. Oil fuels progress, development and the growth of modern civilisation; it is the supreme metaphor of modernity itself."]},{"k":"p","s":["The story of modernity is one of violent struggles and inequalities, and oil has left its unctuous residue across every aspect of economic, political, social and cultural life, often with disastrous consequences."]},{"k":"h","s":["A radical career"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sinclair was born in 1878 – in the first decade that fossil fuels “provided more energy to societies than traditional photosynthesis”, as literary critic Michael Tondre ",["has noted","https://www.theparisreview.org/blog/2023/03/01/oil-on-the-petro-novel/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["His childhood in Baltimore, Maryland, coincided with a period of increasing economic inequality and ",["labour wars","https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/americanexperience/features/theminewars-labor-wars-us/"]," across the US. He likened his family life to “a series of Cinderella transformations” between scarcity and comfort, depending on whether his father, an alcoholic liquor salesman, “had the money for that week’s board”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lifting himself out of poverty by writing dime novels, Sinclair increasingly sought to educate himself about the labour struggles that were rumbling around the nation in the 1890s. He began contributing to various socialist magazines while undertaking postgraduate studies in New York, before turning in earnest to the political writing for which he would be remembered."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sinclair produced an ",["astonishing quantity","https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Author:Upton_Beall_Sinclair"]," of fiction and non-fiction. On several occasions, he ran (unsuccessfully) for public office on a socialist platform. His world was one in which writers could, and often did, hold corporations and governments publicly accountable. He recognised fiction was an especially powerful tool for activism and raising class consciousness."]},{"k":"p","s":["“Great literature”, he reflected in his ",["Autobiography","https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/66840"],", had historically been “a product of the leisure classes and defends their position, whether consciously or by implication”. But literature, he claimed, was becoming “a weapon in the class struggle – of the master class to hold its servants down, and of the working class to break its bonds”."]},{"k":"p","s":["The publication of ",["The Jungle","https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/140"]," (1906) established Sinclair as a force to be reckoned with. A muckraking novel about the Chicago stockyards, The Jungle showed how the meatpacking industry’s unsanitary conditions and brutal exploitation of immigrant workers were enabled by corrupt capitalists with local politicians in their pockets."]},{"k":"p","s":["The novel “aimed at the public’s heart”, Sinclair later quipped, but “by accident I hit it in the stomach”. The backlash prompted by his revelations forced president Theodore Roosevelt to endorse a ",["Pure Food and Drug Act and Meat Inspection Act","https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/changes-science-law-and-regulatory-authorities/part-i-1906-food-and-drugs-act-and-its-enforcement"]," in 1906, to assure the public that adulterated or spoiled food was not being sold to consumers."]},{"k":"p","s":["America’s rich and powerful learned to take seriously the threat posed by Sinclair’s pen. This earned him the esteem of many major left-wing intellectuals of the day, including Eugene Debs, Jack London and Albert Einstein."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sinclair used his profits from The Jungle to establish a utopian commune, ",["Helicon Home Colony","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helicon_Home_Colony"],", in New Jersey, which unfortunately burned down in 1907."]},{"k":"h","s":["Human nature in the raw"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sinclair would go on to write ",["King Coal","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Coal"]," (1917), which took up the cause of unionising coal miners, though it went largely unnoticed. It was Oil!, the third of his major industrial novels, in which he took up his most ambitious theme. In intricate detail, Sinclair set out to dramatise the supply chain through which crude oil is extracted from the earth, refined, stored, transported, produced and sold to the consumer as a commodity."]},{"k":"p","s":["The novel was conceived in 1921, when Sinclair witnessed the Shell Oil corporation strike a 35-metre geyser near his wife’s property in Long Beach, California. Overnight, investors swarmed, trying to cash in on the liquid gold rush. “It was human nature in the raw,” Sinclair recalled, “and this was the first time I had seen it completely naked”:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cliques were formed, and tempers blazed – they never quite came to blows, but almost. And there sat a novelist, watching, listening, and storing away material for what he knew was going to be a great long novel. He listened to the lawyers and to the oilmen who came to make offers; they told their troubles. They wanted the lease as cheaply as possible, and they had no idea they were going to be in a novel with the title Oil! – including the exclamation point."]},{"k":"p","s":["The punctuation mark was necessary to avoid a copyright injunction, but it aptly symbolised the intoxicating process of abstraction that transformed crude oil into a magical substance fuelling our wildest desires and bitterest rivalries. Oil represented mobility, power and the potential to remake the world around our material wants and needs. But it obscured the volatile social processes, struggles and forces involved in its production."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sinclair sought to extend the insights of radical journalistic exposés, including Mary Tarbell’s ",["The History of Standard Oil Company","https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/60692"]," (1904) about corruption in the oil industry. But he believed fiction had powerful advantages over journalism. It could humanise complex political and economic forces, making abstract issues feel comprehensible and relatable."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a contribution to the fight against capitalism, he confided to a family member in 1925, this “oil novel will be the best thing I have ever done”."]},{"k":"h","s":["A radical education"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sinclair’s writing formula was simple and consistent. “Readers of my novels know that I have one favorite theme,” he claimed: “the contrast between the social classes”. There are “characters from both worlds” and plots “contrived to carry you from one to the other”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Beginning in 1912, Oil! is a coming-of-age novel set around Los Angeles, or “Angel City” as it was called. Its young hero, James “Bunny” Ross Jr., is the son of a successful independent oil producer, who is prospecting for new sites to drill."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ross Sr. starts out as an independent entrepreneur, who sees himself as the one of the “little guys” standing up to the big oil companies, including Standard Oil and Shell, who use their money to buy land and political influence to squeeze out competitors."]},{"k":"p","s":["As father and son speed across California, surveying land for suitable tracts to drill, they bribe everyone from highway policemen to local politicians. They seek to turn rocky passes into smooth highways for transporting oil and machinery."]},{"k":"p","s":["Through Bunny’s perspective, Oil! demystifies the commodity’s production. The reader is drawn into the wondrous chemical and engineering feats through which an unrefined substance is blasted out of the earth’s core and refined, beginning a new life as energy for a waxing empire ruled not by any democratically elected government, but an arbitrary handful of men at the helm of a small number of powerful corporations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bunny’s radical education intensifies when he strikes up a friendship with Paul Watkins, the son of an ignorant goatherd whom Ross Sr. swindles by purchasing his land cheaply and renting it back to him, before it is revealed that the fields are saturated with liquid gold."]},{"k":"p","s":["This tract of land, ironically named Paradise, yields a “gusher” of crude right on the eve of World War I. The conflict causes the global demand for fuel to increase exponentially and Ross’ profits skyrocket, launching him into the big league of oil tsardom."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bunny remains loyal to his father, who believes any means justifies the end, because “the world needs oil”. But his moral reservations deepen during a workers’ strike, when his father refuses to distance himself from the underhanded strike-breaking tactics of the corrupt Petroleum Employers’ Federation, including deploying private security firm ",["Pinkertons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinkerton_(detective_agency)"]," to terrorise the workers into submission."]},{"k":"p","s":["The strike leaves the idealistic Bunny with a growing sense reality may not stack up with the education he has received from his father – or from school and university, institutions which, he learns, receive funding from big oil donors, just like many ",["contemporary universities","https://australiainstitute.org.au/report/fossil-fuelled-universities/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["The red millionaire"]},{"k":"p","s":["Paul represents Sinclair’s ideal “incarnation of the new, awakening working class”. He is knowledgeable, loyal, purposeful, courageous. He is, however, conscripted into the US Army and posted to Russia. After the armistice, he is forced with his fellow servicemen to remain there to help crush the revolution. The reason, he discovers, is to prevent the Bolsheviks from socialising the nation’s oil resources and erasing the tsar’s debts to several major American banks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Paul’s example teaches Bunny – and the reader – to see how oil gives limitless influence, control and wealth to the few, while it robs the vast majority of dignity and agency. For many workers, it denies life itself. For every inch of progress oil facilitates, thousands of lives are lost in the rush to build the industry, and in the wars fought to protect reserves and investments."]},{"k":"p","s":["With an awe that is equal parts terror and admiration, Bunny begins to realise the magnitude of what oil represents. He feels obliged to play the role of oil prince. He drives sports cars and dates Hollywood actresses. But he increasingly feels alienated. The press dubs him a “red millionaire”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sinclair enters the capitalists’ world through this internalised class conflict. He shows how they control the circulation of knowledge in universities and newspapers, bribe politicians and lawmakers, pay film executives to produce propaganda demonising revolutionary workers’ movements, and fund religious groups to control their parishioners’ votes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sinclair’s understanding of many of these issues was based on his own observations and experiences. His discussion of Hollywood’s propaganda machine would prove to be prophetic. When Sinclair ",["ran for governor of California","https://depts.washington.edu/epic34/"]," in 1934 on a platform of ending poverty, Irving Thalberg, head of production at Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, attacked him in newsreels that played before every feature film, ",["sinking his campaign","https://www.pbssocal.org/shows/lost-la/the-socialist-who-won-a-democratic-primary-and-the-dirty-hollywood-politics-that-sunk-his-campaign"],". Historian ",["Greg Mitchell has argued","https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/1311425.The_Campaign_of_the_Century"]," the discrediting tactics used against Sinclair were the “birth of media politics”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bunny’s political conversion deepens amid a second larger strike, incorporating more industries this time. He expropriates his father’s profits to try and exonerate imprisoned strikers, including Paul, who has returned to California fully converted to communism."]},{"k":"p","s":["With his comrades, Bunny establishes a radical newspaper to raise consciousness. He funds a night school for organising workers to learn about the class struggle, driving a wedge between him and his father’s world. Like Sinclair, Bunny remains adamant that factional disputes must not distract from the common enemy: capitalism, friend of the fascists, who were already on the march in 1927. This theme would be elaborated in Sinclair’s Pulitzer Prize-winning ",["Lanny Budd series","https://www.goodreads.com/series/64141-lanny-budd"]," of the 1940s and 1950s."]},{"k":"h","s":["Imagining a world without oil"]},{"k":"p","s":["Oil! is a campus novel, a family saga, a Bildungsroman, an engineering manual, a satire of sexual politics, a historical drama, and an anti-capitalist diatribe. It highlights the fact that oil touches every aspect of modernity. No aspect of modern society escapes the torrential flow of Sinclair’s imagination. The novel covers oil-related themes, such as the rise of the automobile industry, and less obviously connected themes, such as Prohibition, religious revivalism, the rise of Hollywood, spiritualism, and the birth-control movement."]},{"k":"p","s":["The pleasure of a Sinclair potboiler is not its aesthetic polish, but immersing oneself in the immense ideas materialising on the page in a great “gush of words”, as Sinclair himself put it."]},{"k":"p","s":["At 550 pages, Oil! is a slow-burner. But its rougher edges are offset by moments of sublime intensity, including this one early in the novel, when an accident causes the Paradise well to erupt in flames – a moment memorably captured in Anderson’s film:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mountains of smoke rose to the sky, and mountains of flame came seething down to the earth; every jet that struck the ground turned into a volcano, and rose again, higher than before; the whole mass, boiling and bursting, became a river of fire, a lava flood that went streaming down the valley, turning everything it touched into flame, then swallowing it up and hiding the flames in a cloud of smoke."]},{"k":"p","s":["This vitality plays an important part in training the reader to feel toward oil and those who manipulate it, moving from wonder and fear to disgust and hate."]},{"k":"p","s":["As in all Sinclair novels, the narrator converts the protagonist’s moral lesson into a didactic message: we must recognise oil as the abstraction of “evil Power” that leads “nations to destruction by visions of unearned wealth, and the opportunity to enslave and exploit labor”. We must continue in our belief there will be utopia after capitalism, because everything is on the line and, in the ",["words of Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels","https://www.marxists.org/archive/marx/works/1848/communist-manifesto/ch04.htm"],", which became Sinclair’s motto, “there is a world to win”."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no simple way to visualise what 100 million barrels of oil burning looks like, but this is approximately how much oil the world burns ",["every 24 hours","https://www.statista.com/markets/410/topic/444/fossil-fuels/#overview"],". Nor is it easy to comprehend the 42 billion tonnes of carbon dioxide emissions that enter our atmosphere in a ",["single year","https://www.theworldcounts.com/earth/climate/global-co2-emissions"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is no simpler to imagine what it will take to break free of fossil fuels. It must surely take the end of market-driven, profit-based mode of production. Yet, as philosopher ",["Fredric Jameson","https://theconversation.com/fredric-jameson-the-worlds-greatest-marxist-critic-is-dead-long-live-utopia-240104"]," once remarked, it “is easier to imagine the end of the world than to imagine the end of capitalism”. To his credit, Sinclair teaches us that we must always rise to that imaginative challenge."]}],"chars":14287},"https://theconversation.com/westpacs-new-hazard-risk-reports-should-sound-a-warning-for-nz-homeowners-296695":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T23:41Z","sha":"229929ef5d94f19c9dd23e1e2a8990431f5a45a3d68e8106877f232da28988cb","read":"https://theconversation.com/westpacs-new-hazard-risk-reports-should-sound-a-warning-for-nz-homeowners-296695","bytes":181523,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Westpac’s new hazard risk reports should sound a warning for NZ homeowners","by":[{"n":"Rohan Havelock","r":"Lecturer, Faculty of Law, University of Auckland, Waipapa Taumata Rau"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T22:39:57Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Westpac’s ",["recent decision","https://www.westpac.co.nz/about-us/media/westpac-nz-adds-natural-hazard-risk-information-to-home-lending-conversations/"]," to share information about natural hazard risks with would-be homebuyers should help them make more informed decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the move has another, potentially more significant, implication: those risks may influence Westpac’s lending decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under the new policy announced last week, home loan applicants will receive a report assessing a property’s exposure to hazards such as flooding, landslides and coastal erosion, using the same data Westpac considers in its lending decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The bank says","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/environment_climate/2523806/westpac-to-factor-natural-hazard-risk-into-mortgage-decisions"]," it doesn’t expect to decline applications solely on the basis of this risk, although in “no more than two [percent] of cases” it may affect the amount it is willing to lend or the duration of the loan."]},{"k":"p","s":["That may seem reassuring, but the estimate reflects Westpac’s present approach rather than the longer-term consequences of increasing natural hazard risks. As banks and insurers become more selective, buying and selling homes in higher-risk areas could become increasingly difficult."]},{"k":"p","s":["Already in New Zealand, ",["an estimated 750,000 people","https://niwa.co.nz/news/nationwide-study-reveals-escalating-flood-risk"]," and NZ$235 billion worth of buildings are potentially exposed to flooding from one-in-100-year rainfall events. With 3°C of global warming – a level the world could reach this century under high-emissions scenarios – those figures could rise to 900,000 people and $288 billion."]},{"k":"h","s":["Hurdles for homebuyers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Homebuyers already face two potential obstacles: obtaining mortgage finance and securing home insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["These obstacles are related because banks generally require properties securing mortgages to be adequately insured. But insurers are increasingly assessing natural hazard risks when deciding whether to provide cover, what premiums to charge and what conditions to impose."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are already signs of this happening. In September 2025, AA Insurance ",["stopped accepting","https://www.odt.co.nz/business/aa-stops-offering-new-policies-in-high-risk-parts-of-canterbury-qdriuasg"]," new home insurance policies in parts of Canterbury because of earthquake exposure. Similar restrictions were reported in ",["Westport","https://www.stuff.co.nz/home-property/360931024/insurer-temporarily-halts-new-policies-westport-due-flood-risk"]," and ",["Blenheim","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/585844/major-insurer-declines-new-home-insurance-policies-for-blenheim"]," this year, amid concerns about flood risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although the Canterbury restriction ",["was subsequently lifted","https://www.waimakariri.govt.nz/council/news-and-information/2026/04/advocacy-results-in-aa-insurance-lifting-canterbury-pause-in-cover"],", and existing policies were generally unaffected, these decisions illustrate how insurers are becoming increasingly selective about the risks they accept."]},{"k":"p","s":["A homebuyer might obtain mortgage approval, only to discover that adequate insurance is unavailable or prohibitively expensive. Alternatively, insurance may be obtainable, but the bank may be unwilling to lend enough to complete the purchase, due to its own assessment of the risk. Either problem could prevent a transaction proceeding."]},{"k":"p","s":["The consequences also extend to existing homeowners. Mortgage agreements generally require borrowers to maintain insurance. Under Westpac’s ",["published standard mortgage conditions","https://assets.dam.westpac.co.nz/is/content/wnzl/dist/lending/all-lending/All-Lending_Memorandum-of-Mortgage_terms-and-conditions_01Jun23.pdf"],", failure to maintain the required insurance can constitute an event of default. That could potentially expose a borrower to enforcement action, even where repayments are up to date."]},{"k":"p","s":["As mortgage finance and insurance become harder to obtain, high-risk properties may become less attractive to prospective purchasers, reducing demand and placing downward pressure on their values."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Reserve Bank ",["this year warned","https://www.rbnz.govt.nz/financial-stability/financial-stability-report/financial-stability-reports/2026/may/financial-stability-report-May-2026/web-version"]," that declining insurance availability could prompt banks to restrict lending in high-risk areas, potentially depressing property values. Conversely, demand for properties in lower-risk areas could increase, pushing their prices higher."]},{"k":"p","s":["Importantly, these effects can arise without a natural disaster actually happening. The growing recognition of a property’s exposure to flooding, erosion or earthquakes may been enough to affect its insurability, access to finance and market value."]},{"k":"p","s":["For existing homeowners, the consequences could be significant. They may find their properties increasingly difficult to sell – or worth substantially less – because of circumstances largely beyond their control."]},{"k":"h","s":["Is NZ’s regulatory framework adequate?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although heavily regulated, banks and insurers are generally free to decide which risks they accept."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no general legal obligation on a bank to provide mortgage finance or on an insurer to insure a particular property. Nor would imposing such obligations necessarily be desirable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Banks and insurers must manage their financial exposures. Forcing them to accept excessive risks could discourage participation in an already relatively small market, ultimately reducing the availability of finance and insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the positive side, their decisions may help stop further investment in high-risk locations, reducing future exposure to losses."]},{"k":"p","s":["All of this raises difficult policy questions. If increasing numbers of homeowners find their properties difficult to insure, finance or sell, should the government intervene to assist them? And if so, what form should that assistance take?"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are several possibilities. One is to help homeowners reduce their exposure through measures such as improved drainage, flood protection or seismic strengthening."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other countries provide useful examples. In Australia, ",["Queensland","https://www.qld.gov.au/housing/buying-owning-home/homeowners-financial-help/resilience-to-floods-and-cyclones/resilient-homes-fund/overview/about"]," and ",["New South Wales","https://www.nsw.gov.au/departments-and-agencies/nsw-reconstruction-authority/reconstruction/resilient-homes-program/about-program"]," have offered programmes for flood-affected homeowners. In the US, California has provided ",["targeted grants","https://www.crmp.org/our-seismic-retrofit-programs"]," to help homeowners make their properties more earthquake-resistant."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another option is to share the financial risks through a form of public insurance not dependent on private insurance, insurance subsidies, or other forms of public assistance. Where properties cannot be protected economically, restrictions on further development or assistance with relocation may be necessary."]},{"k":"p","s":["These options involve difficult trade-offs. Public assistance imposes costs on taxpayers, while requiring banks or insurers to accept greater risks could ultimately reduce the availability of finance and insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["But as natural hazard risks become more fully reflected in lending and insurance decisions, New Zealand will need to confront the consequences for prospective purchasers, existing homeowners and the wider property market."]}],"chars":5940}};
